        {
          "fact": "F5",
          "source": "def-pi-via-first-positive-cosine-zero",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Let $\\gamma$ be the unique smallest positive zero of cosine supplied by [[thm-cosine-has-a-smallest-positive-zero]]. Define\n$$\\pi:=2\\gamma.$$\n\nThus $\\pi>0$ and $\\pi/2=\\gamma$.",
