          "fact": "F6",
          "source": "def-cg-dual-chambers-and-reflection-hyperplanes",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Let $S$, $m$, $V$, $B$, $W$, $\\rho$, $\\Phi$ be as in [[def-cg-canonical-reflection-homomorphism]], and let $V^*$ be the algebraic dual of $V$ ([[def-algebraic-dual-and-linear-functional]]).\n\n**(1) The dual action.** For $w\\in W$ and $f\\in V^*$ define $w\\cdot f\\in V^*$ by $$(w\\cdot f)(v):=f(\\rho(w)^{-1}v).$$ This is the dual (contragredient) action of $\\rho$; that it really is a left action by linear maps is proved in [[lem-cg-dual-action-and-chamber-faces-exist]]. **The dual action is used even when $B$ is degenerate**: no identification of $V$ with $V^*$ through $B$ is made or assumed.\n\n**(2) Chambers, faces, root hyperplanes.** The **closed chamber** is $C:=\\{f\\in V^*:f(e_s)\\ge0\\text{ for all }s\\in S\\}$, its **interior** is $C^\\circ:=\\{f\\in V^*:f(e_s)>0\\text{ for all }s\\in S\\}$, and for $I\\subseteq S$ the **face** $C_I$ is $$C_I:=\\{f\\in V^*:f(e_s)=0\\text{ for }s\\in I\\text{ and }f(e_s)>0\\text{ for }s\\notin I\\},$$ the set of functionals of $C$ vanishing exactly on $I$. For a root $\\alpha\\in\\Phi$ the **root hyperplane** is $H_\\alpha:=\\{f\\in V^*:f(\\alpha)=0\\}=\\ker(\\mathrm{ev}_\\alpha)$, the kernel of the evaluation functional $f\\mapsto f(\\alpha)$ ([[def-kernel-and-image-of-a-linear-map]]).\n\nNeither the nonemptiness of the $C_I$ nor any orbit or tiling property is asserted here; existence of the faces and the exact rank-two chamber structure are proved in [[lem-cg-dual-action-and-chamber-faces-exist]].",
          "uses": [
            "1.2",
            "2.1",
            "2.2",
            "3.2",
            "6.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F6",
          "source": "lem-cg-dual-action-and-chamber-faces-exist",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "**(3) Rank two.** Let $s\\ne t$ in $S$ and put $P:=\\mathbb Re_s+\\mathbb Re_t$. Let $P^*:=\\mathrm{Hom}(P,\\mathbb R)$ be the algebraic dual space of the $2$-dimensional space $P$ ([[def-algebraic-dual-and-linear-functional]]), with the dual basis $f_s,f_t$ of the basis $(e_s,e_t)$ of $P$; functionals on $P$ are the restrictions of functionals on $V$. Let $W_{s,t}:=\\langle\\rho(s),\\rho(t)\\rangle\\subseteq\\mathrm{GL}(V)$ be the matrix subgroup generated by the two reflections. It preserves $P$. For $g\\in W_{s,t}$ and $\\varphi\\in P^*$ define $(g\\cdot\\varphi)(v):=\\varphi(g^{-1}v)$ for $v\\in P$; this is a left action of $W_{s,t}$ on $P^*$ by linear maps, the contragredient of its restriction to $P$. The abstract subgroup $\\langle s,t\\rangle\\le W$ acts through its image $W_{s,t}$; no action of all of $W$ on $P^*$ is asserted. Writing $c:=c(s,t)$ (so $c=1$ for $m(s,t)=\\infty$) and coordinates $(y_s,y_t)$ on $P^*$, so that $\\varphi=y_sf_s+y_tf_t$ and $\\varphi(e_s)=y_s$, $\\varphi(e_t)=y_t$, the dual generators act by $$\\rho(s)^*(y_s,y_t)=(-y_s,\\ 2cy_s+y_t),\\qquad \\rho(t)^*(y_s,y_t)=(y_s+2cy_t,\\ -y_t);$$ each is an involution fixing the line $\\{\\varphi:\\varphi(e_s)=0\\}=\\{y_s=0\\}$ pointwise, respectively $\\{\\varphi:\\varphi(e_t)=0\\}=\\{y_t=0\\}$, and the functional $\\delta(\\varphi):=\\varphi(e_s+e_t)$ is preserved by $W_{s,t}$ when $m(s,t)=\\infty$. For $\\beta\\in P$ the rank-two root hyperplane is $H_\\beta\\cap P^*:=\\{\\varphi\\in P^*:\\varphi(\\beta)=0\\}$, and $\\Phi_P:=W_{s,t}\\{e_s,e_t\\}\\subset P$ is the rank-two root system.\n\n(i) If $m:=m(s,t)<\\infty$: $W_{s,t}$ is a dihedral group of order $2m$, and the $2m$ chambers $wC_P$ ($w\\in W_{s,t}$), where $C_P:=\\{f\\in P^*:f(e_s)\\ge0,\\ f(e_t)\\ge0\\}$, are exactly the $2m$ closed sectors cut out in $P^*$ by the $m$ root hyperplanes $H_\\beta\\cap P^*$ $(\\beta\\in\\Phi_P)$, $\\Phi_P:=W_{s,t}\\{e_s,e_t\\}$. They have pairwise disjoint interiors, their union is all of $P^*$, $W_{s,t}$ acts simply transitively on them, and any two distinct chambers are separated by at least one root hyperplane, i.e. there is $\\beta\\in\\Phi_P$ with the two interiors in opposite open half-planes of $H_\\beta$.\n\n(ii) If $m(s,t)=\\infty$: the chambers $wC_P$ ($w\\in W_{s,t}$) have pairwise disjoint interiors and their union is $\\{\\varphi\\in P^*:\\varphi(e_s+e_t)>0\\}\\cup\\{0\\}$, that is, the closed half-plane $\\{\\varphi:\\varphi(e_s+e_t)\\ge0\\}$ with the nonzero points of its boundary line removed; any two distinct chambers are separated by at least one root hyperplane $H_\\beta\\cap P^*$ $(\\beta\\in\\Phi_P)$, and the traces $H_\\beta\\cap\\{\\varphi:\\varphi(e_s+e_t)=1\\}$ are exactly the integers in the coordinate $y_s$ on that affine line.",
          "uses": [
            "1.2",
            "2.1",
            "2.2",
            "3.2",
            "6.1"
          ]
